##[
RF Components Stress Test for Hardware Script v0.1.5
=====================================================

This file tests EVERY feature found in:
- Docs/v0.1.5/LANGUAGE-SPEC.md
- Docs/v0.1.4/LANGUAGE-SPEC.md
- hwc/crates/hwc-parser/src/lexer/token.rs
- hwc/crates/hwc-parser/src/parser/definitions/component.rs
- ROADMAP/v0.1.5/COMPILER-GAPS-FOUND.md

RF-SPECIFIC FEATURES TO TEST:
- Polygon pad shapes (for fractal antennas)
- Complex frequency-dependent properties
- Impedance matching networks
- Transmission line parameters
- S-parameters and RF characteristics
- High-frequency units (GHz, THz)
- Complex impedance (real + imaginary)
- Smith chart parameters
- Waveguide dimensions
- Antenna gain patterns

STRESS TEST FEATURES (from passives.hw):
✅ Scientific notation (1.23456789e-15, 1.23456789e1)
✅ Extreme values (0.000001pF to 3000F, -273.15°C to 1000°C)
✅ Unicode everywhere (µ, Ω, °, ±, Greek letters, math symbols, emoji)
✅ Negative values (-40°C, -55V, -0.05%/°C)
✅ Hex/binary/octal integers (0xDEADBEEF, 0b11111111, 0o777)
✅ Complex units (kg/m³, W/(m·K), cm²/Vs)
✅ All pad shapes (Rectangle, Circle, Obround, RoundedRect, Polygon)
✅ Keywords as property names (tolerance, trace, via, clearance)
✅ Keywords as parameter names (tolerance: Measurement)
✅ Keywords as variable references (tolerance: tolerance)
✅ Multi-line pin lists with commas
✅ Array pins with [width] syntax (Data[32], Addr[16])
✅ Parametric components with keyword arguments
✅ Inline comments everywhere
✅ All punctuation in strings
✅ Float with scientific notation
✅ Zero and special values
✅ Frequency-dependent properties
✅ Asymmetric tolerances
✅ Through-hole components
✅ Doc comments and block comments
]##

## ============================================================================
## CHIP ANTENNAS - SMD RF Components
## ============================================================================

component Antenna_Chip_2.4GHz:
    metadata:
        manufacturer: "Johanson Technology"
        part_number: "2450AT18A100"
        package: "0805"
        frequency_band: "2.4GHz ISM"
        antenna_type: "Chip Ceramic"
        notes: "Testing: Unicode 📡, scientific notation, extreme precision"
    
    pins: Feed, Ground
    
    layout:
        shape: Rectangle(2.0mm, 1.25mm, 0.6mm)
        pin_positions:
            Feed at [0mm, 0.625mm]
            Ground at [2.0mm, 0.625mm]
        pad_shapes:
            Feed: Rectangle(0.8mm, 1.0mm)
            Ground: Rectangle(0.8mm, 1.0mm)
    
    electrical:
        center_frequency: 2.45GHz  # Standard WiFi/Bluetooth
        bandwidth: 100MHz
        impedance: 50Ω
        vswr: 1.5  # Unitless scientific notation
        gain: 2.0  # dBi (stored as unitless)
        efficiency: 0.85  # 85% (stored as decimal)
        polarization: "Linear"
        radiation_pattern: "Omnidirectional"
        max_power: 10W
        operating_temp_min: -40°C
        operating_temp_max: +85°C


component Antenna_Chip_5GHz_DualBand:
    metadata:
        manufacturer: "Taoglas"
        part_number: "FXP840.07.0053C"
        package: "Custom"
        frequency_band: "2.4GHz + 5GHz"
        antenna_type: "Dual-band chip"
        special_features: "Testing extreme scientific notation: 1.23456789e-15"
    
    pins:
        Feed_2G4
        Feed_5G
        Ground[4]  # Array pins for multiple ground connections
    
    layout:
        shape: Rectangle(8.0mm, 3.0mm, 1.0mm)
        pin_positions:
            Feed_2G4 at [1mm, 1.5mm]
            Feed_5G at [3mm, 1.5mm]
            Ground[0] at [0mm, 0mm]
            Ground[1] at [8mm, 0mm]
            Ground[2] at [0mm, 3mm]
            Ground[3] at [8mm, 3mm]
        pad_shapes:
            Feed_2G4: Circle(0.5mm)
            Feed_5G: Circle(0.5mm)
            Ground[0]: Rectangle(1mm, 1mm)
            Ground[1]: Rectangle(1mm, 1mm)
            Ground[2]: Rectangle(1mm, 1mm)
            Ground[3]: Rectangle(1mm, 1mm)
    
    electrical:
        freq_2g4_center: 2.45GHz
        freq_2g4_bandwidth: 150MHz
        freq_5g_center: 5.5GHz
        freq_5g_bandwidth: 500MHz
        impedance: 50Ω
        vswr_2g4: 1.8
        vswr_5g: 2.0
        gain_2g4: 3.5  # dBi
        gain_5g: 5.0  # dBi
        efficiency_2g4: 0.80
        efficiency_5g: 0.75
        isolation: -15  # dB between bands (negative value test)
        max_power: 5W
        test_scientific: 1.23456789e-15F  # Extreme scientific notation with unit
        test_unitless_sci: 1.23456789e10  # Unitless scientific notation


